course: dictionary
lesson: 5436
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A stone stuck beside it can make a horse lame, so that it limps.» Here lame means unable to walk normally because a leg or foot is hurt.
explain: Lame can also be slang. «That joke is lame» has nothing to do with legs. Nobody's leg is hurt by a joke; it means the joke is boring or not cool. Read the words around lame, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: A lame excuse is a weak one that nobody believes. Lame is a word to use carefully. Describing a person who cannot walk well as lame is old-fashioned and can hurt their feelings. Say «has a limp» or «cannot walk easily» instead.
fact: Lame means unable to walk normally because a leg or foot is hurt.
fact: Lame is used most often about animals, especially horses.
fact: «That joke is lame» is informal slang meaning boring or not cool.
fact: A lame excuse is a weak one that no one believes.
fact: Using lame about a person is old-fashioned and can be hurtful; say «has a limp» instead.
exercise: «The horse went lame after it stepped on a stone.» What does lame mean here? | Very funny and full of jokes | Angry with its rider | *Unable to walk normally because of a hurt leg | Tired after a long race
exercise: «That film was so lame.» What does lame mean here? | Wet and muddy | Very loud | *Boring and not cool | Walking with a limp
exercise: What is a lame excuse? | A very clever excuse | *A weak excuse that no one believes | A long story about a dog | An excuse about a horse
test: What does a lame horse find hard to do? | Sleep in a stable | Run across a field | *Walk normally | Eat its food
test: Which is the kinder way to describe a person who walks with a limp? | Lame | *Has a limp | Broken | Slow and boring
exam: Which meaning of lame fits «Like a broken tooth or a lame foot is reliance on the unfaithful in a time of trouble»? | Boring and not cool | Very funny | A weak excuse | *Hurt, unable to walk well
